{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/928030-mnesis-quests","id":928030,"title":"Mnesis quests.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-08T02:57:06-07:00","id":928030,"title":"Mnesis quests.","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> Could you please, guys, tell me about the Mnesis quests? I have a Mokole character in my group, and his player announced that he will seek advice in Mnesis, which sounds very close to a Mnesis quest to me. But what is a Mnesis quest? I haven't really got the idea of umbral quests (appreciate if you show me a couple of examples of them), and a Mnesis quests makes even less sense to me.<br /> <br /> Bearing in mind that W20 is poor in case of mechanics, I have read Mokole breedbook (2nd edition) and PG to Changing breeds (rev. edition), but couldn't gain any useful ideas from them. So, please, advice on the Mnesis quest topic or at leas how to implement Umbral quest's ideas for Mnesis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11161-leeder","name":"Leeder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T04:16:34-07:00","id":928050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leeder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/928030-mnesis-quests#post928030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello!<br /> <br /> Could you please, guys, tell me about the Mnesis quests? I have a Mokole character in my group, and his player announced that he will seek advice in Mnesis, which sounds very close to a Mnesis quest to me. But what is a Mnesis quest? I haven't really got the idea of umbral quests (appreciate if you show me a couple of examples of them), and a Mnesis quests makes even less sense to me.<br /> <br /> Bearing in mind that W20 is poor in case of mechanics, I have read Mokole breedbook (2nd edition) and PG to Changing breeds (rev. edition), but couldn't gain any useful ideas from them. So, please, advice on the Mnesis quest topic or at leas how to implement Umbral quest's ideas for Mnesis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mnesis quests are about rites that take you back into memories and get you to live through them or experience them through the eyes of your ancestor. They're an excellent way to add historical notes and characters to the plot. I've found it best to simply start the rite and then include the other PC's as the supporting cast to the mnesis delving ancestor (usually with conspiciously similar character sheets, since you might want to pull it off on the fly).<br /> <br /> To date I've used Mnesis quests quite a bit, be it for tracking the path of the Sword of Plagues and how it was lost, I've triggered it when they were diving into a sunken city that the character was lost for a moment between the time the city was above ground and he was a great priest in it. It's brilliant to find stories, characters, histories and context that pertain to the current crisis. Say you want an old weapon, rite or exploration of led to a war between two septs? Or heck, you just feel like an Arabian Nights Werewolf?<br /> <br /> It's loads of fun, and it opens tons of options. Just consider how history could affect and influence your story, and then allow the characters to live through it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T04:52:16-07:00","id":928061,"title":"","content":"Thank you, Asmodai! But what about mechanics of the quests? Is a Quest a normal short adventure, running in a different setting, or it has a set of different rules, like that of an Umbral realm's? Does the dreamng character realize what is going on, or it is a story of an ancestor, like in Assasin's Creed game series?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11161-leeder","name":"Leeder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T07:51:09-07:00","id":928125,"title":"","content":"It depends on how much work you want to put into a mnesis quest. Do you want to create new character sheets for all the players to be the cast in the memories or do you want to just assume that the ancestors are oddly just like the player characters for simplicity like Asmodai said? you can have a mnesis quest be quick (relatively) and to the point, or you can have it be a large part of the arc. The dreaming character can get caught up in the memory and lose place of where they are (The film &quot;the giver&quot; actually has a scene where the giver gets lost in a Vietnam flash back), but in many cases they are aware they are trying to remember what their ancestors experienced like Assassin's creed. As for rule sets like the umbral realms, I'd argue there isn't necessarily different rules when in the mnesis itself, unless they are remembering being in other realms. Now going into the deep umbra to retrieve new memories, that's a whole different story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T04:20:13-07:00","id":929655,"title":"","content":"Thank you, guys, for your suggestions!<br /> <br /> I have implemented that approach to mnesis quests, and my players highly acclaimed that feature with Assasin's Creed-like sub-game. I will definitely use it again when the circumstances are suitable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11161-leeder","name":"Leeder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T11:46:01-07:00","id":929863,"title":"","content":"There aren't really any mechanics. It's a narrative framework, and down to you to decide how it will work. Let us know when you figure out what it will be like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T11:57:30-07:00","id":929872,"title":"","content":"I'm glad they're into Assassin's Creed, you could definitely center arcs around this, heck they could have enough fun that you end up with an all Mokole game before long!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T04:36:44-07:00","id":930276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/928030-mnesis-quests?p=929872#post929872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm glad they're into Assassin's Creed, you could definitely center arcs around this, heck they could have enough fun that you end up with an all Mokole game before long!</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that you need all the characters to be Mokole for it to work. One is enough, and through a rite he can lead the others into the roles of people who were around his ancestor...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T15:45:50-07:00","id":930558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/928030-mnesis-quests?p=930276#post930276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not that you need all the characters to be Mokole for it to work. One is enough, and through a rite he can lead the others into the roles of people who were around his ancestor...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh I just meant soon you get some &quot;ME TOO&quot; if an idea is popular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}